WEBVTT

00:01:28.738 --> 00:01:30.756
But there were problems.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:32.473
One problem

00:01:32.473 --> 00:01:35.106
is there are some sounds in Arabic

00:01:35.106 --> 00:01:38.105
that just don't make it through a European voice box

00:01:38.105 --> 00:01:40.372
without lots of practice.

00:01:40.372 --> 00:01:42.106
Trust me on that one.

00:01:42.106 --> 00:01:44.323
Also, those very sounds

00:01:44.323 --> 00:01:46.237
tend not to be represented

00:01:46.237 --> 00:01:49.825
by the characters that are available in European languages.

00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:51.639
Here's one of the culprits.

00:01:51.639 --> 00:01:53.523
This is the letter sheen,

00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:57.122
and it makes the sound we think of as SH -- "sh."

00:01:57.122 --> 00:01:59.724
It's also the very first letter

00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:02.156
of the word shayun,